# Icon Import Convention (`~icons`)

This project generates tree-shakeable React SVG icons from Iconify JSON into `src/icons/` via `bun run generate-icons`. Imports keep the unplugin-style path and work with Turbopack (no webpack plugin).

Required packages: `@iconify/utils`, and the relevant `@iconify-json/*` packs (`mdi`, `solar`, `octicon`, …).

## Required

```typescript
import AccountIcon from '~icons/mdi/account.jsx';
import GiftIcon from '~icons/solar/gift-bold.jsx';
```

After adding a new `~icons/...` import, run:

```bash
bun run generate-icons
```

## Forbidden

```typescript
import AccountIcon from '~icons/mdi/account';
import GiftIcon from '~icons/mdi/gift-outline.tsx';
import { Icon } from '@iconify/react'; // client-only; skips SSR
```

## Rules

- Always use the `~icons/<set>/<icon-name>.jsx` import path.
- Always end the import with `.jsx` — never omit the extension or use `.ts`/`.tsx`.
- Import icons as default exports and render them as components: `<AccountIcon />`.
- Place icon imports in a dedicated `// Icons` block, matching existing project style.
- Do not hand-edit files under `src/icons/` — regenerate with `bun run generate-icons`.
